{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792352304,"nonce":"GX2R+WceuyLnTMrqXrUe81Xx3/I=","title":"Explorer of an extension project lists only its source folders","message":"For a project with a `.rayext`, the Explorer shows the config and the folders named in `sources`. A file elsewhere in the project, such as a README.md at the root, has no row, so it has no context menu and an extension cannot contribute an item to it.\n\nThe Markdown fixture lists `docs` in `sources` for this reason. The Explorer should show the project folder as it is (hidden folders and build output left out), the way an editor's does, for extension projects at least.","files":null}]}